From e71a37538e4edcb3c50e7a26e34c5b2cdd1d9023 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jelle Feringa <jelleferinga@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:47:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Throw instead of dereferencing null collision data before
 update()

The collision constraints assign collision_data_ only in update(), and their
getters dereferenced it unchecked, so getValues()/getJacobian() on a linked
constraint before the first update() crashed. They now throw
std::runtime_error("<name>: collision data not computed, call update() first").
This covers the discrete, continuous and numerical constraints, and the
getJacobian() of the D variants (their getValues() returns cached values).

Closes #617
